alwaysApply: true
---

This repo has a graphify knowledge graph of `src/` at `docs/architecture/graphify-out/` (symlink: `graphify-out/`).

For architecture, dependency, or "how does X connect to Y" questions, prefer graphify before broad Grep sweeps:

```bash
G=.tools/graphify-venv/bin/graphify
GRAPH=docs/architecture/graphify-out/graph.json
$G query "<question>" --graph "$GRAPH"
$G path "<A>" "<B>" --graph "$GRAPH"
$G explain "<concept>" --graph "$GRAPH"
$G affected "<symbol>" --graph "$GRAPH"   # name must uniquely match a node
```

If the venv is missing: `python3 -m venv .tools/graphify-venv && .tools/graphify-venv/bin/pip install -U pip graphifyy`

- Start with `docs/architecture/graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for broad orientation
- Prefer `GRAPH_TREE.html` over `graph.html` when opening in a browser (lighter)
- After large structural edits, rebuild with `scripts/update-graphify.sh`
- For incremental updates: `$G update src` — do NOT pass `--graph` (not a valid option), and do NOT pass `.` (scans the whole repo root)
- `graphify <subcommand> --help` is unreliable; use `$G --help`
- Skill details: `.ai/skills/graphify/SKILL.md`

Ordinary line-level edits and targeted Read/Grep do not need a graphify pass first.
